Let the bindings serialize the log without going through a file.
The undo history (cpp/bindings/history.cpp) keeps logbook states as the XML that
would be saved. save_dives() only writes to a path, and the buffer it writes from
is static; a temporary file per edit would be disk writes for nothing, and a way
for an edit to fail on a full disk. Removes `static`, and changes nothing else.

--- a/core/save-xml.cpp	2026-11-06 18:07:37
+++ b/core/save-xml.cpp	2026-11-06 18:07:37
@@ -637,7 +637,7 @@
 	put_format(b, "</site>\n");
 }
 
-static void save_dives_buffer(struct membuffer *b, bool select_only, bool anonymize)
+void save_dives_buffer(struct membuffer *b, bool select_only, bool anonymize)
 {
 	put_format(b, "<divelog program='subsurface' version='%d'>\n<settings>\n", dataformat_version);
 
